<title>USA: Commerzbank near buying U.S. fund business -- report.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank near buying U.S. fund business -- report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerzbank AG is close to buying the $7.4 billion mutual fund business of San Francisco investment bank Montgomery Securities, Business Week magazine reported.</p>
<p>It quoted a source close to the matter as saying a deal was &quot;fairly imminent&quot; but that details, including the selling price, were still being ironed out.</p>
<p>The Montgomery Asset Management business manages 19 no-load mutual funds.</p>
<p>Neither side would confirm the deal, Business Week said.</p>
